From 010168643276e933f4cd60624c353f0f57661789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmad Jalil <ahzs645@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:43:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(indoor): faster exact rational arithmetic with identical
 values

Replace the Euclid gcd in the vendored exact-arithmetic module with a Rust
binary gcd compiled to WebAssembly (source in vendor/native-rational-gcd) and a
Lehmer fallback, reduce sums and products on small operands, and add
floating-point filters for compare and orient2d that defer to exact arithmetic
whenever a result does not clear its error bound.

Two full campus compiles compared value by value: 11,802,992 values, 0
differences. Export byte identity of a master is not yet measured. The module
stays byte-identical to the OpenIndoorMaps copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
